01:56:28,000 --> 01:56:30,000
So, there might be something like that out there.

288
01:56:30,000 --> 01:56:36,000
But, again, my experience is mathematical economists are generally bored

289
01:56:36,000 --> 01:56:40,000
by common sense observations that invalidate big claims.

290
01:56:40,000 --> 01:56:44,000
Like, they're much more interested in very technical refinements

291
01:56:44,000 --> 01:56:47,000
within a very narrow context.

292
01:56:47,000 --> 01:56:48,000
And if you were to say, look, you know,

